        content: `You have a Table named \`tblDepartments\` with a column \`Name\` containing department names. You want a dropdown in cell B2 that lets the user pick from the Name column, and the dropdown should **auto-expand** when new departments are added to the table.

In the Data Validation dialog, Allow = List. What do you enter for Source?`,
        question: "What's the correct Source for a Table-backed dropdown that auto-expands?",
        options: [
          { text: "=tblDepartments[Name]", correct: false },
          { text: "=INDIRECT(\"tblDepartments[Name]\")", correct: true },
          { text: "=NAMED(tblDepartments.Name)", correct: false },
          { text: "tblDepartments.Name", correct: false }
        ],
        explanation: "The correct answer is **`=INDIRECT(\"tblDepartments[Name]\")`**. Excel's Data Validation dialog **doesn't directly accept structured references** — you'll get an error or silent refusal if you try `=tblDepartments[Name]` directly. Wrapping the reference in **INDIRECT** with the reference as a *text string* makes Excel evaluate it at runtime, and this happens to also bypass the validation restriction. Bonus: because INDIRECT re-evaluates on each click, the dropdown automatically picks up new rows added to the table. Option C uses a function that doesn't exist. Option D is dot syntax from another language. Option A is the natural-looking attempt that Excel rejects.",
        visual: {
          type: "diagram",
          svg: `<svg viewBox="0 0 1100 1100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="55" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="32" font-weight="bold" font-family="Arial">Table-Backed Dropdown Quiz</text><text x="550" y="95" text-anchor="middle" fill="#888" font-size="18" font-family="Arial">Get the dropdown to auto-expand with the table</text><rect x="80" y="130" width="450" height="380" fill="none" stroke="#6366f1" stroke-width="2"/><text x="100" y="160" fill="#6366f1" font-size="18" font-weight="bold" font-family="Arial">tblDepartments</text><rect x="80" y="170" width="450" height="40" fill="#6366f1" opacity="0.3"/><text x="120" y="197" fill="#ffffff" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" font-family="monospace">Name</text><line x1="80" y1="210" x2="530" y2="210" stroke="#6366f1"/><line x1="80" y1="245" x2="530" y2="245" stroke="#444"/><line x1="80" y1="280" x2="530" y2="280" stroke="#444"/><line x1="80" y1="315" x2="530" y2="315" stroke="#444"/><line x1="80" y1="350" x2="530" y2="350" stroke="#444"/><line x1="80" y1="385" x2="530" y2="385" stroke="#444"/><line x1="80" y1="420" x2="530" y2="420" stroke="#444"/><text x="120" y="232" fill="#ffffff" font-size="15" font-family="monospace">Engineering</text><text x="120" y="267" fill="#ffffff" font-size="15" font-family="monospace">Sales</text><text x="120" y="302" fill="#ffffff" font-size="15" font-family="monospace">Marketing</text><text x="120" y="337" fill="#ffffff" font-size="15" font-family="monospace">Finance</text><text x="120" y="372" fill="#ffffff" font-size="15" font-family="monospace">Operations</text><text x="120" y="407" fill="#ffffff" font-size="15" font-family="monospace">Legal</text><text x="120" y="450" fill="#10b981" font-size="14" font-style="italic" font-family="monospace">(type "Data Science" here -&gt; auto-add)</text><rect x="570" y="130" width="450" height="380" fill="#1a1a2e" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="2"/><text x="795" y="165" text-anchor="middle" fill="#10b981" font-size="18" font-weight="bold" font-family="Arial">Cell B2 dropdown</text><rect x="590" y="190" width="410" height="50" fill="#1a1a2e" stroke="#666"/><text x="610" y="220" fill="#ffffff" font-size="16" font-family="monospace">Engineering</text><polygon points="975,210 990,210 982,225" fill="#888"/><rect x="590" y="240" width="410" height="220" fill="#1a1a2e" stroke="#666"/><rect x="590" y="240" width="410" height="32" fill="#6366f1" opacity="0.3"/><text x="610" y="262" fill="#ffffff" font-size="15" font-family="monospace">Engineering</text><text x="610" y="294" fill="#ffffff" font-size="15" font-family="monospace">Sales</text><text x="610" y="326" fill="#ffffff" font-size="15" font-family="monospace">Marketing</text><text x="610" y="358" fill="#ffffff" font-size="15" font-family="monospace">Finance</text><text x="610" y="390" fill="#ffffff" font-size="15" font-family="monospace">Operations</text><text x="610" y="422" fill="#ffffff" font-size="15" font-family="monospace">Legal</text><text x="610" y="455" fill="#10b981" font-size="15" font-family="monospace">Data Science  &lt;-- auto-added</text><rect x="80" y="540" width="940" height="200" fill="#1a1a2e" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="2"/><text x="100" y="575" fill="#ef4444" font-size="18" font-weight="bold" font-family="Arial">What FAILS:</text><rect x="100" y="595" width="900" height="40" fill="#ef4444" opacity="0.15" stroke="#ef4444"/><text x="115" y="622" fill="#ef4444" font-size="15" font-family="monospace">Source: =tblDepartments[Name]</text><text x="100" y="660" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14" font-family="Arial">Excel rejects structured references directly in Data Validation Source.</text><rect x="100" y="675" width="900" height="40" fill="#ef4444" opacity="0.15" stroke="#ef4444"/><text x="115" y="702" fill="#ef4444" font-size="15" font-family="monospace">Source: tblDepartments.Name      Source: =NAMED(...)</text><rect x="80" y="770" width="940" height="300" fill="#1a1a2e" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="2"/><text x="100" y="805" fill="#10b981" font-size="18" font-weight="bold" font-family="Arial">What WORKS:</text><rect x="100" y="825" width="900" height="50" fill="#10b981" opacity="0.15" stroke="#10b981"/><text x="115" y="855" fill="#10b981" font-size="16" font-family="monospace">Source: =INDIRECT("tblDepartments[Name]")</text><text x="100" y="900" fill="#ffffff" font-size="15" font-family="Arial">- The structured reference is now a TEXT STRING inside INDIRECT().</text><text x="100" y="930" fill="#ffffff" font-size="15" font-family="Arial">- INDIRECT resolves the string to a live range at evaluation time.</text><text x="100" y="960" fill="#ffffff" font-size="15" font-family="Arial">- Each click on the dropdown re-runs INDIRECT -&gt; auto-grows with the table.</text><text x="100" y="1010" fill="#ffd700" font-size="15" font-style="italic" font-family="Arial">Mental model: Data Validation only accepts ranges or named refs.</text><text x="100" y="1040" fill="#ffd700" font-size="15" font-style="italic" font-family="Arial">INDIRECT turns a text string into a "range" it accepts.</text></svg>`,
          caption: "Direct table refs are rejected. INDIRECT wraps them as text — and gives you auto-expand for free."
        }
