        title: "The Six-Step Build Plan",
        content: `**Step 1 — Skeleton.** New workbook. Create four sheets via Shift+F11: **Inputs**, **Categories**, **Summary**, **Dashboard**. **Step 2 — Categories tab.** Type the list (Rent, Utilities, Food, Gas, Entertainment, Savings, Other) in A2:A8. Select → Ctrl+T to make it a **Table** named **tblCategories**. Define a **named range** CategoryList = =tblCategories[Category]. **Step 3 — Inputs tab.** Create two Tables: **tblIncome** (Date, Source, Amount) and **tblExpenses** (Date, Category, Description, Amount). On the Category column apply **Data Validation → List → =CategoryList**. **Step 4 — Number formats.** Format Amount columns as **$#,##0.00;[Red]-$#,##0.00**. **Step 5 — Summary tab.** Build the monthly variance using **SUMIFS** over tblExpenses. Apply **conditional formatting**: highlight red when Spent > Budget. **Step 6 — Sheet replication + print.** Right-click Summary → Move/Copy → Create a copy × 11 to make Jan–Dec. Set **Print Area**, **Print Titles ($1:$1)**, footer **&F | &A | Page &P of &N**. Save as **.xltx**.`,
